From a92289eb775f31eae7ac0a05796c03876f746e8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Krish Paul <me@krishnendu.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 02:55:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] tools/video-probe: the measurements behind the video
 player's limits

fbprobe times full-panel RGB565 frames into the framebuffer with no
decoder in the loop; decprobe decodes a clip with libavcodec, converts
each frame to RGB565 and reports the time of every stage against the
clip's frame rate. make-clips.sh encodes one source at four sizes in
five codecs to run them against.

On the R1, per 30 fps frame, decode plus conversion:

            320x180  480x270  640x360  800x450
  MPEG-2      4.6      9.0     16.1     25.2  ms
  MPEG-4      5.2     10.3     18.5     29.0
  H.264 BP    9.6     20.2     37.5     59.9
  H.264 HP   11.3     21.1     39.8     66.0

The host ffmpeg is built with --disable-asm: with only --disable-x86asm
its scaler writes noise, and every clip comes out at the right size and
bitrate with nothing in it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
